I collapsed the null-check and validity-check into a single conditional expression, eliminating the early-return branch and keeping the field pointer in one expression so the compiler emits a tighter sequence. The returned value is bit-identical to the original in every case.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsTimestampValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(253);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
```